{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfs2ZL52u17ak1sYVXLEP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The root cause is visible now. `today = now.date()` takes the date in UTC, not in `tz`. For 23:30 UTC on June 1 (01:30 June 2 in Berlin), the candidate is built as June 1 01:00 Berlin. That is in the past, so the code adds 24 hours in UTC. The result is still before `now` (June 2 01:00 Berlin is 23:00 UTC), and the function never re-checks it. The DST symptom has the same source: adding 24 UTC hours across the March transition shifts the wall-clock time by an hour. I'll fix both by working in the zone's local calendar and advancing by calendar days, not elapsed hours."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9469,"cache_read_input_tokens":24487,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9469},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cd8f5570-4c48-414d-a9a2-f7d71224c929","uuid":"63760fa4-827d-42b0-89d9-5f5bbf201807","timestamp":"2026-10-09T17:05:38.613Z","request_id":"req_011Cfs2ZKmgf3VW9f5c5qqus"}
